From 9791ac666aad1c273cd4c46721ccf2abedae7ee4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duchil6063 <duchil6063@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:52:14 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] itasha: composition family and character name text in the
 Itasha menu

Two entries the engine grew: [Composition Family] pins which grammar the
side decoration is composed in (auto builds every family as a candidate and
keeps the best-scoring one), and [Character Name Text...] opens a dialog
for the name, a title, style, placement, priority, outline, shadow, a layer
cap and the game-font fallback, then runs the "text" action. [Remove Text]
runs "no-text". The last text input is kept in QSettings itasha/text/* so
the dialog reopens with it. Strings go to the engine as single QProcess
arguments, so spaces and case survive. Korean entries for every new string.
---
